label: Direct County Query
description: >-
  A parcel query addressed to a county's own ArcGIS FeatureServer, with no
  intermediary. Osceola, Manistee and Roscommon resolve this way.

  This edge exists ONLY to make the trust boundary a type. In blue-ribbon the
  distinction is invisible: `getCountyAdapter(county)` returns a
  `CountyParcelAdapter`, and all five implementations satisfy the same
  interface, so nothing in the type system says Iosco's parcels transit a
  commercial proxy and Osceola's do not. Splitting the query into two edges is
  the single clearest win weir produced in this exercise.
fields:
  pin:
    classification: linkable
    type: utf8
    label: PIN
    description: The parcel identification number being queried
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 8
      maxLength: 40
  county:
    type: utf8
    label: County
    description: The county whose FeatureServer is being queried
    nullable: false
    enumValues:
      - Osceola
      - Manistee
      - Roscommon
  endpoint:
    type: utf8
    label: Endpoint
    description: >-
      The county FeatureServer query URL. Verified-provenance source: the
      county is the authoritative publisher of its own parcel geometry.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 10
      maxLength: 500
